The latest MSTest is **4.3.0**. Here are the breaking changes that affect your project:

## 1. `[ExpectedException]` is removed (critical for your code)

Your two tests using `[ExpectedException(...)]` will fail to compile. Replace with `Assert.ThrowsExactly<T>`:

```csharp
// Before
[ExpectedException(typeof(ArgumentNullException))]
[TestMethod]
public void Validate_NullInput_ThrowsArgumentNull()
{
    Validate(null);
}

// After
[TestMethod]
public void Validate_NullInput_ThrowsArgumentNull()
{
    Assert.ThrowsExactly<ArgumentNullException>(() => Validate(null));
}
```

## 2. Analyzer MSTEST0032 becomes a **warning** (affects your code)

`Assert.IsTrue(true)` in `Validate_ValidInput_Succeeds` will trigger a warning about always-true conditions.

## 3. Other notable v4 breaking changes (not directly hitting your code, but good to know)

| Change | Impact |
|--------|--------|
| `Assert` APIs no longer accept `message` + `params object[]` — use string interpolation | Only if you use format strings in assertions |
| `ClassCleanupBehavior` enum removed | Only if you specify `EndOfAssembly` |
| `TestContext.Properties` is now `IDictionary<string, object>` | Only if you use `.Contains()` → change to `.ContainsKey()` |
| Minimum TFM is net8.0 (net6/7 dropped) | You're already on net8.0 ✓ |
| `TestMethodAttribute.Execute` → `ExecuteAsync` | Only if you have custom test method attributes |

---

Would you like me to apply the migration changes to your project files?
